      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The outcome of 200 consecutive patients with inguinal hernias repaired by the tension-free mesh technique at a specialist clinic was assessed one year after operation. There were no recurrences and no major complications. The wound infection rate was 1%. Less than 10% of patients had only minor complaints and 99% of patients were satisfied or very satisfied with the operation and its outcome. Low recurrence rates after one year imply low long-term recurrence and testify to the benefits of a specialist approach."},
